  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "I always seem to misplace my keys or my phone at the worst time, right before I have to walk out the door. I put on my shoes, grab my bag, and then realize the keys aren't in my pocket. Any calm I had just goes away. I start looking all over the place. I check the table, digthrough  the sofa cushions, and even peek into the fridge. My mind runs through what I did a few minutes ago. Did I set my phone down by the sink? Did it slip off the counter? I get annoyed and a little stressed because I'm already running late. I tell myself every time that I'll drop my keys in the same spot so I won't lose them, but something always seems to distract me and I forget. Eventually, I find what I'm looking for, often somewhere obvious, and I laugh at myself. It's a tiny thing that always throws me off, but it's part of everyday life.",
      "start_time": 0.079,
      "end_time": 52.979,
